5,1,1,talk,Midori,,I worry about who is actually in charge when things break. Let’s see if the plan survives contact with reality.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,The depot floor doesn’t stop for office projects. I need to know if our equipment can handle whatever we choose.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,May,,I’m suspicious of systems that age quietly or come back broken from outside. Let’s check the history of our upgrades.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Misaki,,We are understaffed. I need to see how the last rollout landed on the people who actually do the work.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,Headline prices lie. I want to see the invoices that keep arriving after the contract is signed.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, the floor is critical, but without clear ownership, even good tools fail. Let’s verify the support structure.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, agreed. But if the yard devices can’t talk to the new system, the floor stops. I’ll check the hardware.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, the invoices are key. I’ll look at the upgrade history to see if we’ve been stuck in the past.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, history is useful, but I need to know if our admins can even learn the new system. I’ll check the hiring times.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, hiring is slow, but the money is the real trap. I’ll examine the renewal invoices and the board minutes.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Midori,,I’ll look into the support ownership during the last outage and the warehouse rule changes. I need to know who is responsible.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,I’ll examine the depot calendar and the yard devices. We need to know if the system fits our actual operations.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,May,,I’ll review the upgrade history of the dispatch tool and the data lift from the 2018 pay move. I want to see the patterns.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Misaki,,I will review the administrator retirements and the depot supervisors from the last rollout. I need to understand the human cost.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,I will examine the five years of renewal invoices and the board minutes on capital requests. I need to see the true cost.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Midori,,I’m glad we’re covering the human and operational sides. I’ll stick with my two choices to understand the support gaps.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,I’m ready to see if the hardware can survive the change. Let’s hope the data is clear.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,May,,I’ll stick with my two choices. Understanding the past failures is the only way to avoid repeating them.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Misaki,,"I’ll stick with my two choices. The people are the bottleneck, not the software.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,Agreed. The data will show where the money actually goes. I’ll review my findings before we vote.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
