31,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Midori,,The support was unowned for two days last winter. And the warehouse rules changed twice in a year. The plan is fragile.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The peak season has no freeze window. And the yard devices are a mess of old models. A cutover now is a disaster.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,The dispatch tool skipped three upgrades. And the 2018 data lift had errors for a year. We are stuck in the past.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Two admins retire this year, and the last posting was open for eleven months. The supervisors dropped the new routines quickly.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The bundled agreements held price, but the add-ons climbed yearly. The board trimmed capital but let operating costs run.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, the lack of a freeze window is terrifying. If we can’t stop the floor, we can’t change the system.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, exactly. And the devices won’t talk to each other. We need a system that works with what we have, not what we wish for.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, the climbing add-ons are a trap. We need a fixed cost, not a subscription that grows every year.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, the hiring gap is real. If we can’t find admins, we can’t maintain any complex system. We need simplicity.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, simplicity is good, but if the operating costs keep rising, we’re dead. I need to see a vendor with a fixed, predictable bill.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, a fixed bill is essential. But if the support is scattered, we’re still in trouble. We need one throat to choke.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, agreed. One vendor, one support line. And it has to work with our old yard devices.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, if it works with our old devices, it’s probably not modern. But maybe that’s what we need. Stability over novelty.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, stability is key. But if the admins can’t learn it, it’s useless. We need something they can actually manage.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, I agree. A system that is too complex will fail because we can’t staff it. We need a balance.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I’m leaning towards a vendor that offers a single, integrated support model. It reduces the risk of unowned outages.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I’m looking for a system that can be deployed without a full freeze. Maybe a phased approach?,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,I’m wary of modular systems. They seem to age in place. I prefer a suite that is maintained as a whole.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I’m concerned about the training burden. If the supervisors drop the routines, the system fails. We need strong onboarding.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I’m focused on the total cost of ownership. A fixed configuration process might be the only way to keep the costs down.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
