60,3,1,talk,Midori,,The candidates are here. Meridian offers a hosted suite with a regional team. That sounds like the single support line I need.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Tessera is a subscription with a marketplace. That sounds like the climbing add-ons Benjamin warned about. I’m not keen.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,Corvus is modular. That’s exactly the pattern I saw in the dispatch tool. It ages in place. I’m avoiding it.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Anchor is built for transport and deployed on our servers. But if our admins are retiring, can we maintain it?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Meridian’s fixed configuration process appeals to me. It might stop the operating costs from climbing.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, Tessera’s marketplace is a risk. We’ve seen how add-ons climb. I’m sticking with Meridian for its integrated support.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, I agree. But what about the yard devices? Can Meridian work with our old scanners?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, if Meridian is a hosted suite, it might handle the device integration better than a modular system.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, but who maintains it? If it’s hosted, maybe the vendor handles the device compatibility? That would help my team.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, if the vendor handles the maintenance, it reduces our staffing burden. That’s a win for both of us.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, exactly. Meridian’s regional team can handle the support, and the fixed configuration keeps the costs predictable.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, I’m still worried about the peak season. Can Meridian be deployed without a full freeze?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, a hosted suite might allow for a phased rollout. We can test it in one depot first.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, a phased rollout is good. But we need to ensure the supervisors are trained properly. The last rollout failed because they dropped the routines.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, Meridian’s fixed process might include structured training. That could address the supervisor issue.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Midori,,I’m voting for Meridian. It offers the integrated support and fixed costs we need.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I’m voting for Meridian. It’s the safest bet for our hardware and calendar constraints.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,I’m voting for Meridian. It avoids the modular aging trap and the subscription cost creep.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I’m voting for Meridian. The hosted model reduces the maintenance burden on our thin team.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I’m voting for Meridian. The fixed configuration process is the only way to control the long-term costs.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
